    "evidence_text": "We demonstrate the potential of our evaluation framework by evaluating existing image captioning models on a wide ranging set of synthetic datasets that we construct for diagnostic evaluation.\n\nstrengths and limitations of existing models.\n\nWe use ShapeWorld to generate training and evaluation data for two major reasons.\n\nGTD Evaluation Framework ::: Truthfulness\tThe second aspect we investigate is truthfulness,\n\nTable TABREF4 gives an overview for different ShapeWorldICE datasets we use in this paper.\n\nWe consider three different types of captioning tasks, each of which focuses on a distinct aspect of reasoning abilities.\n\nExistential descriptions examine whether a certain object is present in an image.\n\nQuantification descriptions involve count-based and ratio-based statements, with an explicit focus on inspecting models for their counting ability.\n\nEach dataset variant consists of around 200k training instances and 4,096 validation instances, plus 4,096 test instances.\n\nAt test time, only the test images are available to the evaluated models.\n\nUnderlying world models are kept from the models and are used for later GTD evaluation.\n\nFor each test instance, we sample ten reference captions of the same distribution as the training captions to enable the comparison of our proposed metrics to BLEU",
